# LeakSanitizer suppressions for G-LSAN (.port/tools/gates/sanitizers.sh --gate lsan).
#
# Every entry here is a THIRD-PARTY leak (a system library or vendored C we do
# not own). Each one has a row in .port/phase-2/SANITIZER_SUPPRESSIONS.md with
# its cited reason and evidence, and a WHY comment directly above it (D6 rule c,
# d6_cfg_mapping_audit.py). A leak in Rustty code is never suppressed: it is a
# finding (an N id, and a UD if Ghostty has it too).
#
# Format: one `leak:<pattern>` per line; the pattern matches a function, source
# file or module name anywhere in the leaking allocation's stack.
